7 Reading sessions: how words rise by themselves
************************************************

You do not have to set every level by hand.  bltzread also promotes
words as you read:

  1. You read part of the text.
  2. You tell bltzread which part you read.  This is a "finish": press
     ‘s f’, or answer the question when you close the buffer.  A program
     that closes the buffer for you can call ‘bltzread-offer-record’
     first; it asks once, and the question is not repeated on close.
  3. Every word in that part that you did not look up gets one "clean
     read".
  4. When a word has enough clean reads it moves up one level.  How many
     it needs depends on the level (see
     ‘bltzread-promotion-thresholds’).
  5. A word you looked up during the session loses its clean reads and
     keeps its level.

   A level you set by hand always wins over this automatic climbing.

   Press ‘C-u s f’ to finish and mark everything in the range as known
at once.

