11.1 Language and words
=======================

‘bltzread-bltzr-executable’
     Name or path of bltzr.  Default ‘bltzr’.
‘bltzread-bltzr-extra-args’
     Extra arguments for every bltzr call.
‘bltzread-default-language’
     Language used when a buffer has none.  Nil means ask.
‘bltzread-word-regexp’
     What counts as a word.
‘bltzread-word-regexp-alist’
     A different word pattern for particular languages.
‘bltzread-track-by’
     ‘form’ keeps a level for each spelling.  ‘lemma’ keeps one level
     for a basic word and all its forms.
‘bltzread-skip-numerals’
     Never mark a token with no letter in it.  Default yes.
‘bltzread-make-read-only’
     Make the buffer read-only while the mode is on.  Default yes.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Levels,  Next: Skip lists,  Prev: Language and words,  Up: Options

11.2 Levels
===========

‘bltzread-promotion-thresholds’
     Clean reads needed to climb from level 1, 2, 3 and 4.  Default 3 3
     4 5.
‘bltzread-count-each-occurrence’
     Count a word every time it appears in the range, instead of once
     per session.
‘bltzread-lookup-effect’
     What a lookup does: ‘reset-reads’, ‘demote’ (also lose a level), or
     ‘nothing’.
‘bltzread-level-scope’
     ‘word’ (default): setting a level changes every form of the word.
     ‘form’: only that spelling.
‘bltzread-lookup-counts’
     What counts as a lookup: ‘command’ (only ‘l’, the default),
     ‘interaction’ (‘l’, ‘d’, ‘D’, ‘s .’), or ‘popup’ (the automatic
     card, but only after ‘bltzread-lookup-dwell’ seconds on the word).
‘bltzread-lookup-dwell’
     Seconds the card must stay on a word before it counts, for ‘popup’.
     Default 1.5.
‘bltzread-unknown-max-level’
     Words at or below this level are "unknown" for the jump keys.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Skip lists,  Next: Storage,  Prev: Levels,  Up: Options

11.3 Skip lists
===============

‘bltzread-known-write-policy’
     ‘unset’ (default): acts as ‘review’ and warns once per session that
     you have not chosen.  ‘review’: words wait in the queue.
     ‘immediate’: written the moment they reach level 5.
‘bltzread-warn-known-write-unset’
     Set to nil to silence that warning.  Better: choose a policy.
‘bltzread-list-target’ and ‘bltzread-list-target-alist’
     Which list receives known words, overall and per language.
‘bltzread-skip-exact-words-files’ and ‘bltzread-skip-word-families-files’
     Your own file names per language.
‘bltzread-bltzr-config-file’
     Which bltzr settings file to read.
‘bltzread-skip-lists-count-as-known’
     Treat words already on the lists as level 5.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Storage,  Next: Card and dictionary,  Prev: Skip lists,  Up: Options

11.4 Storage
============

‘bltzread-state-directory’
     Folder for the state files.
‘bltzread-save-delay’
     Seconds of idle time before saving.
‘bltzread-history-limit’
     How many finished sessions to remember.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Card and dictionary,  Next: Keys,  Prev: Storage,  Up: Options

11.5 Card and dictionary
========================

‘bltzread-popup-trigger’
     ‘point’ (automatic) or ‘manual’.
‘bltzread-popup-delay’
     How long the cursor must rest first.
‘bltzread-popup-only-on-motion’
     Open a card only after a command moved point onto a word.  Default
     yes.
‘bltzread-popup-scroll-hook’
     Runs, with the window selected, after the card scrolled the window
     to make room (the card is always above the word).  A package that
     follows the window's start can use it to tell this scroll from
     yours.
‘bltzread-popup-gap’
     Space between word and card in lines.  Nil means 0.75.
‘bltzread-popup-hide-after-set’
     Hide the card after a level change.  Default yes.
‘bltzread-popup-style’
     ‘auto’, ‘box’, ‘side-window’ or ‘echo’.
‘bltzread-popup-show-gloss’
     Show the dictionary entry in the automatic card.
‘bltzread-popup-max-lines’, ‘bltzread-popup-lookup-max-lines’, ‘bltzread-popup-width’
     Card size.
‘bltzread-dictionary-function’
     Your own lookup function.
‘bltzread-sdcv-executable’, ‘bltzread-sdcv-dictionaries’, ‘bltzread-sdcv-data-dir’
     The sdcv program, which dictionaries per language, and the folder
     holding them.
‘bltzread-sdcv-data-dir-alist’
     A different dictionary folder for particular languages, for example
     one holding a fixed copy of the Pāḷi dictionary.
‘bltzread-dict-filters’
     Short entries for the card: per dictionary (or language), which
     pieces of the entry to show, as a regexp, a ‘:class’ plist or a
     function.  The lookup key still shows the whole entry.  bltzread
     ships no dictionary-specific code.  See the tutorial section _Short
     dictionary entries_ and the docstring.
‘bltzread-sdcv-unlisted-languages’
     ‘none’ (default) or ‘all’: what a language missing from
     ‘bltzread-sdcv-dictionaries’ searches.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Keys,  Next: Reading sessions,  Prev: Card and dictionary,  Up: Options

11.6 Keys
=========

‘bltzread-prefix-key’
     The prefix.  Default ‘s’ (the same one-letter prefix subtle uses).
     Nil for none.
‘bltzread-direct-keys’ and ‘bltzread-direct-key-bindings’
     The single keys such as ‘1’ and ‘l’.  Turn them off if they clash
     with another mode.
‘bltzread-mouse-lookup-key’
     Mouse gesture for lookup.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Reading sessions,  Next: Pasted text,  Prev: Keys,  Up: Options

11.7 Reading sessions
=====================

‘bltzread-prompt-on-close’ and ‘bltzread-min-chars-for-prompt’
     Ask to record reading when the buffer closes, but only after enough
     text was passed.  ‘bltzread-offer-record’ asks once, whoever closes
     the buffer.
‘bltzread-bookmark-policy’ and ‘bltzread-bookmark-name-function’
     Whether and how the bookmark moves.
‘bltzread-undo-limit’
     How many changes ‘u’ can take back.  Default 200.
‘bltzread-range-method’, ‘bltzread-range-confirm’
     How the range is chosen.
‘bltzread-range-farthest-source’
     What counts as having reached a place in ‘farthest’: ‘window-end’
     (default), ‘point’, or a function returning a position (or nil).
‘bltzread-range-start-function’
     Function returning where the ‘farthest’ range begins; nil for the
     usual start.


