12 Using bltzread with subtle
*****************************

subtle plays audio or video in mpv and shows its subtitles as text.  No
bridge package is needed; these settings make the two compose:

Setting                                                               Effect
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘bltzread-range-farthest-source’ ‘#'subtle-played-through-position’   Reading credit ends where playback has reached.
‘bltzread-range-start-function’ ‘#'subtle-played-start-position’      Credit starts where the latest continuous run of playback began.  Seeking or pausing by hand does not count as
                                                                      reading.
‘subtle-buffer-setup-hook’                                            Turn ‘bltzread-mode’ on for track index 0 only (the track you study); the other stays plain.
‘subtle-pause-hook’                                                   Runs when you pause by hand: start ‘bltzread-avy-unknown’.

     (setq bltzread-range-farthest-source #'subtle-played-through-position
           bltzread-range-start-function  #'subtle-played-start-position)

     (add-hook 'subtle-buffer-setup-hook
               (lambda ()
                 (when (= subtle-track-index 0)
                   (setq bltzread-language subtle-language) ; from movie.sl.srt
                   (bltzread-mode 1))))

     (add-hook 'subtle-pause-hook
               (lambda () (when bltzread-mode (bltzread-avy-unknown))))

   Keep ‘subtle-scroll-style’ at ‘paged’: continuous scrolling carries a
word away while you look it up (subtle warns about it).  The first load
of a big transcript takes a moment, because bltzr is called once for all
its words.  subtle's ‘subtle-hold-functions’, ‘subtle-anchor-functions’
and ‘subtle-dismiss-functions’ are set for you by subtle once bltzread is
loaded, so a card holds the page and ‘q’ closes it first.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Limits,  Prev: Using bltzread with subtle,  Up: Top

13 Limits
*********

   • Single words only; phrases are not tracked.
   • Basic forms come from bltzr and are looked up again in each Emacs
     session.
   • Nothing is shared between languages.


